{
  "additional_concerns": [
    "Footnote 7 confines the holistic assessment to exposure below 50%. The OR formula preserves the known classification outcome above that threshold; the footnote does not establish that an operative designation ceases when exposure changes.",
    "FALSE requires affirmative absence of both routes, not merely failure to establish either route. It establishes neither non-complex status nor historical declassification nor permission to sell.",
    "Global conflict blocking is an execution policy additional to the circular. It can block evaluation despite an independently established route; it must not be interpreted as a contrary legal classification.",
    "Exposure measurement, LAF identification and designation verification are delegated judgments. Correspondence of the Boolean formula does not validate these inputs.",
    "The prior disagreement about BDCs reflects two scopes: upstream exposure identification and the formula consuming an already assessed exposure fact. The proposal below uses the exact typed question while retaining that upstream relevance.",
    "The representation preserves an unrestricted aggregate exposure input but does not expressly implement review of subsequent SFC updates. The open-ended scope and update mechanism therefore have different correspondence outcomes.",
    "The supplied missing dependency IDs have no identifying metadata. None can safely be mapped to a named authority.",
    "The separate LAF circular, UT Code paragraph 7.3, internal product approval circular and Advertising Guidelines are not supplied. They would be needed for their respective broader regulatory questions, but are not additional prerequisites to this Boolean classification test."
  ],
